      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This article presents strategies for enhancing the emergency department care delivered to patients with chest pain and suspected acute myocardial infarction. It also describes the planning and implementation of an emergency department reengineering project at a university medical center. The establishment of chest pain evaluation centers within emergency departments has been associated with improved clinical outcomes and cost control. Creating such a center requires careful revamping of diagnostic and treatment algorithms, a process that must be based on information from all departments affected by the changes."},
